+#### Max Losing Streak
+
+`MaxLosingStreak` looks at trades within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), ordered from most-recent to oldest, and counts an unbroken run of losing trades (a trade with `close_profit` below `required_profit`, which defaults to 0.0). As soon as a winning trade is found, the count stops - unlike `StoplossGuard` or `LowProfitPairs`, a win in between resets the streak instead of just diluting a total.
+
+If `trade_limit` or more losing trades happened in a row for a pair, that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+This applies across all pairs at the same time (a bot-wide losing streak also stops new entries everywhere), unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time.
+
+The below example stops trading for a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` defaults to false, for the whole bot) for 4 candles once 3 losing trades happened in a row within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxLosingStreak",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    A single winning trade breaks the streak - `trade_limit` therefore counts *consecutive*
+    losses, not the total number of losses within `lookback_period`.
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
